      content:
          '**Vitals**: BP 158/92 mmHg, HR 88 bpm, RR 16, SpO2 98% on RA, Temp 36.8C, BMI 31.\n\n**General**: Tearful female in loose-fitting clothing. Right sleeve draped loosely — grimaces and withdraws when sleeve brushes her arm. Appears fatigued and distressed.\n\n**Neurological**:\n- **Mental Status**: Alert, oriented x3. Flat affect with intermittent crying. Speech fluent without aphasia.\n- **Cranial Nerves**: Right lower facial droop (mild, residual). Right-sided facial allodynia — withdraws from light touch to right cheek.\n- **Motor**: Right upper extremity 4-/5 throughout. Right lower extremity 4/5 throughout. Left side 5/5. Mildly increased right-sided tone (Modified Ashworth 1).\n- **Sensory**: **Right side** — Profound allodynia (cotton wisp produces 8/10 burning pain). Hyperalgesia (pinprick produces 10/10 pain with radiation). Decreased proprioception at right toes and fingers. Temperature dysesthesia — both warm and cold stimuli produce burning pain. **Left side** — intact to all modalities.\n- **Coordination**: Right-sided dysmetria on finger-to-nose (mild — related to sensory impairment more than cerebellar dysfunction).\n\n**Musculoskeletal**: Right shoulder mildly subluxed (1 finger-breadth). Limited right shoulder ROM — 90 degrees flexion, 80 degrees abduction (pain-limited, not structural).\n\n**Gait**: Ambulates with quad cane and contact guard assist. Right foot circumduction pattern. Slow, guarded gait — winces with each right foot strike.\n\n**Psychological Observation**: Makes poor eye contact. States twice during exam that she \'cannot go on like this.\' Husband appears exhausted and tearful.',
